cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CollationKit in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "CollationKit: transposition-aware scholarly textual collation"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "ancientlives"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ancientlives/CollationKit"
url: "https://ancientlives.github.io/CollationKit/"
license: MIT
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-09-25"
keywords:
  - textual collation
  - textual scholarship
  - digital humanities
  - critical apparatus
  - sequence alignment
  - variant graph
  - Swift
abstract: >-
  CollationKit is a deterministic, pure-Swift engine for scholarly textual collation.
  It compares several witnesses of one work and reports insertions, deletions,
  substitutions and transpositions (including moves across page boundaries), each
  with a page, line and word citation. It separates substantive from accidental
  variants, supports base-anchored and peer (base-free) multi-witness merges and
  cross-language anchoring, and ships a command-line tool, an interactive HTML
  viewer, and a language-neutral conformance corpus with a JSON Schema.
